    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dd800905_8bb73efe",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/PipelineData.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 524,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-13T16:01:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Now that the FSM\u0027s lifetime goes beyond a single DrawPass, we can\u0027t use a bare pointer as the key anymore.  A DrawPass that adds one SkShader can drop all of its refs to the paint params that keep the shader alive and some new surface\u0027s paints could end up with a new SkShader assigned to the same address depending on what the caller was doing to create its paints.\n\nI believe we proposed adding a unique ID field to SkShaderBase so we could key off of that.  Otherwise we need to change this to `sk_sp\u003cSkGradientBaseShader\u003e` and add a hash function that looks at just the underlying bare address (vs. trying to also factor in the ref count, which I think the default hash would do).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 524,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 524,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "3f062c1a5ab071e357bb074d7ab2591c463e98d1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
